From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 05:45:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] hwcomposer: v20: a protected video plane under the UI

The LuneOS Widevine bridge decodes protected video on the device's secure
decoder, inside the Android container. Those buffers can't be read or drawn
by the GPU, so the only way to show them is as a hardware composer layer of
their own. This adds that layer to the v20 backend.

With QPA_HWC_VIDEO_SOCK set, the backend listens on that unix socket for one
sender at a time. Each message carries a decoder buffer's description and its
file descriptors, plus an optional fence. Each buffer becomes the content of a
DEVICE layer below the UI layer, and the UI layer is blended premultiplied so
the compositor's punch-through hole shows the video. hwc2_compat has no call
for the layer order, so android::HWC2::impl::Layer::setZOrder is looked up in
libhwc2_compat_layer.so.

The compositor tells the plugin where the hole is through the
"videoplanegeometry" native resource: x, y, width, height and rotation, with
width -1 hiding the plane. The picture is fitted into that rect with its
aspect kept, clipped at the panel edges, and rotated by the HWC transform in
landscape. A worker thread applies it, so the GUI thread never waits for a
present. Without QPA_HWC_VIDEO_SOCK the resource is null and nothing changes.

The video layer is set to DEVICE before every validate: a frame placed at a
bad rect falls back to CLIENT, and once accepted that sticks, leaving a black
hole. The sender is another process, so every message is checked (size, fd
count, handle size) and a malformed one is dropped with its descriptors
closed.

The socket is created mode 0666, because the sender runs in the Android
container. Any local process can therefore hand the compositor buffers.

Tested on a Pixel 3a (sargo) with the bridge in Atlas: NPO, Prime Video and
Angel One played on the plane, which followed card moves and rotation.
Malformed messages sent to the running compositor were dropped, with no
crash and no leaked descriptor. The new code builds without warnings for
armv7 and aarch64, and the analysers' findings in it are fixed.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS-specific: the frame protocol and the compositor resource are the Widevine bridge's]
